  "markdown": "Services\n\n# Window film: decorative, privacy, solar and safety\n\nFilms applied to existing glass: frosted and decorative designs, privacy, solar control and safety films for London homes, hotels, offices and shopfronts.\n\n[Start your project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?service=window-film&topic=service%3Awindow-film) [See the work](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/)\n\nWindow film changes how existing glass behaves without replacing it. There are four families. Decorative films give a frosted, etched, gradient or patterned finish, including logos and manifestations. Privacy films screen a view by day, or hide a room completely. Solar control films reduce heat gain and glare. Safety and security films help hold broken glass together.\n\nThe right film depends on the glass, the frame, the orientation and what the room needs. Some films are not suitable for every type of double glazing, so we check the glass and the film maker's guidance before we recommend one.\n\nGlass is cleaned to a high standard, the film is cut to the visible pane and squeegeed out, and edges are finished neatly to the frame. Small moisture haze is normal for a short time while the adhesive cures, and we explain what to expect on the day.\n\nTrained at Solar Screen's headquarters in Luxembourg in window films (Solar Screen) and architectural and furniture wrapping film (Cover Styl'). We install to the maker's instructions. At Hyde London City (the Old Bailey Hotel) we fitted Solar Screen film to the glazing as part of the full decorating package. The same practice surveys, supplies the film if you need it, installs and comes back for aftercare.\n\nMakers: [Solar Screen window films](https://solarscreen.eu/en/), [Cover Styl' architectural and furniture films](https://coverstyl.com/en/)\n\n![Rolls of Solar Screen window film on site before installation.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/old-bailey-15-800.webp)\n\nRolls of Solar Screen window film on site before installation at [Hyde London City](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/). The product is checked before any glazing is covered. Photograph: Dorin Burcus / Mr Wallcover.\n\n01\n\n## Window film on the record\n\nAt [Hyde London City](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/) (the Old Bailey Hotel), Solar Screen window film was fitted to the glazing as part of our full decorating package, alongside paint and specialist wallcoverings, in the Grade II-listed building that opened as a hotel on 2 September 2024.\n\n02\n\n## How a window film job runs\n\nThe survey looks at the glass, the frame, the orientation and what the room needs, and the film maker's guidance decides what can be applied to that glazing. On the day, the glass is cleaned, the film is cut to the visible pane and squeegeed out, and the edges are finished to the frame. A slight haze while the adhesive cures is normal, and we explain what to expect.\n\nRisk assessments and method statements (RAMS) are issued for every package, and Dorin Burcus personally supervises the site. Film can be part of a wider decorating commission, as at Hyde London City, or a job on its own.\n\n## On the public record\n\n[![Sample room at Hyde London City with a Timorous Beasties Tropical Clouded Leopard panel behind the bed.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/old-bailey-06-800.webp)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/)\n\nSample room at Hyde London City with a Timorous Beasties Tropical Clouded Leopard panel behind the bed. Photograph: Dorin Burcus / Mr Wallcover.\n\n### [Hyde London City (the Old Bailey Hotel)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/)\n\nFull decorating package: decoration, specialist wallcoverings and window film, c. 2 years.\n\n[View the project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/)\n\nQuestions\n\n## Questions we are asked\n\nIllustrative material studies\n\nPause motion\n\n### What should I send for a window film quotation?\n\nTell us where the glazing is and whether you need decorative, privacy, solar control or safety film. The glazing type, frames and orientation need to be checked against the film maker's guidance before a product is recommended. Include whether you need film supplied as well as installed.\n\n### Which type of window film do I need?\n\nDecorative or frosted film for screening and design, privacy film to hide a view, solar control film for heat and glare, and safety or security film to help hold broken glass together. Some films combine more than one job. We recommend one after seeing the glass and the room.\n\n### Can window film go on double glazing?\n\nOften, but not every film suits every unit. Solar films in particular can raise the temperature of the glass. We check the glazing type and follow the film maker's guidance on what can be applied.\n\n### Can window film be removed later?\n\nYes. Film can be taken off and the glass cleaned, which makes it useful for rented premises, changing branding or a room that changes use.\n\n### What accreditations or training do you hold?\n\nMr Wallcover trained at Solar Screen's headquarters in Luxembourg in window films (Solar Screen) and in architectural and furniture wrapping film (Cover Styl'), and installs both to the maker's own instructions. Site card and accreditation details are available on request.\n\n### Do you issue RAMS, and who supervises the site?\n\nRisk assessments and method statements (RAMS) are issued for every package, and Dorin Burcus personally supervises the site.\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder\n",
